# The JAM page (the SELECT dial, after Global): the keys are an instrument and never edit the scale. Voice (K1): pluck, pad, acid, drone; Keys (K2): scale, chords,
# harp; Octave (K3); Answer (K4): after you stop it plays your phrase back an octave up on the next bar.
seed 0
wait 3000
tap GLO
expect view 19
spin SELECT 1
wait 100
expect view 20
expect jamv 0
shot jam_pluck.png
# the pad, scale keys: one key, one note held; the scale untouched
spin K1 1
wait 50
expect jamv 1
key 13 down
wait 200
expect held 1
expect pool 0x5AD
shot jam_held.png
key 13 up
wait 100
expect held 0
# chords: three notes
spin K2 1
wait 50
expect jamm 1
key 13 down
wait 200
expect held 3
key 13 up
wait 100
expect held 0
# the harp
spin K2 1
wait 50
expect jamm 2
key 0 down
wait 200
expect held 1
key 0 up
wait 100
expect pool 0x5AD
# the answer: three notes on the pluck, then silence: it keeps them (3), and plays them back on a bar line, then forgets
spin K2 -2
spin K1 -1
spin K4 1
wait 50
expect jamv 0
key 13 down
wait 150
key 13 up
wait 200
key 16 down
wait 150
key 16 up
wait 200
key 20 down
wait 150
key 20 up
wait 100
expect anscnt 3
wait 7000
expect anscnt 0
expect ansplay 0